# DISPLAYED per-tier cells were re-derived from count×prior and never saw that reconciliation.
# Measured baseline (2026-07-12, full clean pools, before this lever): Σcells(mid) != total grid(mid)
# on aisha 109/142 (64% under-claimed + 13% overflowing) and ahmed 352/1418; worst ahmed 2501 R2 has
# a HARD total grid of 154 (== settled truth) whose combo.grids sum to 152, while the display claims
# only 103 — 49 cells belonging to nobody. Centering the display options on the combo's OWN fitted
# grid closes the identity. Gated on total_grid_target being present: without a target the fit is a
# no-op, combo.grids IS the naive count×prior, and the existing display path's partial-floor
# re-centring (2401 R3) is strictly better than inheriting it. Kill: the env below.
